  "notes": {
    "coverage": "Only the NPS/class combinations listed in coverage are represented. Missing combinations are unsupported here; no interpolation or extrapolation is performed.",
    "socketWeldDimensions": "Table 6.1-1 dimension A is center-to-bottom of socket and J is minimum socket depth. This pack retains both raw dimensions separately. Figure 6.2.7-1 illustrates an approximate 1.5 mm recommended pre-weld gap; that recommendation is not used as an exact geometric offset. No socket-mouth, pipe-insertion clearance, weld-gap, or center-to-end distance is derived. The limited ADR-061 application profile separately selects the standard-defined socket-bottom datum and uses tabulated A directly as its port distance; this is an explicit application convention, not a newly derived standard dimension or a socket-mouth location.",
    "threadedDimensions": "Table 6.1-3 gives center-to-end A for 90-degree elbows and center-to-end C for 45-degree elbows.",
    "qualifierSemantics": "Only the explicit bend angles 45 and 90 are represented. B16.11 does not label these table rows long-radius or short-radius.",
    "classDesignation": "B16.11 class designation is a dimensional lookup key here. Do not treat it as the project PMS class or as a directly encoded pressure rating.",
    "scope": "This transcription is limited to two-ended 45-degree and 90-degree elbows. It excludes street elbows (Table 6.1-4), mixed socket-welding/threaded ends, reducing construction, other fitting types, and special dimensions agreed under para. 1.1.2.",
    "unitBasis": "Only the SI millimeter tables are transcribed. The US Customary tables are an independent standard unit system and are not converted or mixed with these values.",
    "limitations": "Table dimensions are nominal and subject to manufacturing tolerances. This reference is not a CAD solid, installation-weld specification, or engineering certification."
